Subject: Volume of each group of sounds
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

The launcher's sound levels are a host audio setting, independent of the
[gameplay] tweak mask (issue #59). Every sound's volume passes through
SoundPlaybackEvent::UpdatePlaybackParameters, the only caller of the sources'
SetInputVolume. There the player's level of the sound's group is added, in
decibels, to the level the game set, down to the game's floor of -96 dB,
which the mixer plays as silence. The group follows the sound's mix category
and its sound bank (src/platform/game_tweaks.cpp). Movie audio is mixed by
THPSimple apart from these sounds; its samples are scaled by the movie level.
With every group at 100 % nothing changes. The guarded hooks exist only in the
opt-in native game module.

